meta {
  name: List the syllabus
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/curricula/{{curriculumId}}/nodes
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.count: eq 2
  res.body.curriculum_nodes[0].id: eq {{curriculumUnitId}}
  res.body.curriculum_nodes[1].id: eq {{curriculumTopicId}}
}

docs {
  Flat, in teaching order: sequence first, then creation order where sequences
  tie. The tree is rebuilt by the caller from parent_id, which is cheaper than
  nesting it here and lets a client show the same nodes as a list, an outline
  or a checklist without asking again.

  Filters are parent_id, kind and status, so a client can ask for one unit's
  children, or for the topics only, without walking the whole syllabus.

  The curriculum itself is checked for reach before the nodes are read: a
  syllabus the caller cannot see is 404, not an empty list of nodes.
}
